Audi MHI2 Virtual Cockpit AltScreen
=================================

CarPlay and Android Auto Altscreen on the Audi Virtual Cockpit.
Nvidia Tegra MHI2 only; not compatible with MHI2Q/Qualcomm.

Supported configuration
-----------------------
Firmware: MHI2_ER_AUG22_K3344 / MU1438
Cluster:  LVDS Virtual Cockpit, classic gauge layout
Platform: Nvidia Tegra, QNX 6.5

Other firmware versions are not validated. Installers verify the exact
component hashes in profiles/mu1438.json.

Status
------
CarPlay:      Working cluster map, automatic takeover and Apple Maps wheel zoom.
Android Auto: Working 1080p cluster stream; 1920x720 map area scaled to 1440x540.
              The paired main-screen configuration is limited to 30 fps.
Pending:      AA wheel zoom, CarPlay native navigation instructions, touchpad,
              album art, additional layouts and extended reliability testing.

The runtime was tested on one vehicle. The consolidated installer has not
been validated as a fresh installation on another car.

Installation
------------
See INSTALL for SSH and M.I.B. SD-card installation, build inputs and rollback.
Project-built native binaries are included in carplay/bin and androidauto/bin.
The compiled HMI add-on and QNX SHA-256 utility are also available:
    https://github.com/aberbic/Audi-MHI2-Virtual-Cockpit-Altscreen-CarPlay-AndroidAuto/releases/tag/mu1438-install-components-20261003

Prepare the baseline bundle without a QNX SDK, Java or Docker:
    python3 scripts/fetch-firmware.py
    python3 scripts/fetch-prebuilt.py
    python3 scripts/prepare-bundle.py --prebuilt

Download helpers require Python 3 and GitHub CLI, or manually downloaded archives.
Component hashes and source revision are in prebuilt/mu1438-components.json.
K3346 is not validated; a differing gal.json still fails the installer checks.

The required MU1438 firmware build inputs are available as a release asset:
    https://github.com/aberbic/Audi-MHI2-Virtual-Cockpit-Altscreen-CarPlay-AndroidAuto/releases/tag/mu1438-build-inputs-20261003

This includes the converted stock HMI JAR. No firmware extraction from the
car is needed for building; installation still verifies the target unit.

Development
-----------
Run host tests without a vehicle or firmware inputs:

    bash scripts/test.sh

Rebuild native components with the configured QNX toolchain:

    bash carplay/scripts/build-native.sh
    bash androidauto/scripts/build-native.sh

Build outputs go to ignored out/ directories. Packaging uses the tested bin/
artifacts, not newly compiled replacements. See INSTALL before changing them.

Source layout
-------------
carplay/       CarPlay hook, video renderer and supervisor
androidauto/   AA video service, renderer and profile tests
hmi/           Shared cluster ownership, labels and control integration
scripts/       Build, bundle, install and validation tools
toolbox/       M.I.B. entry points
touchpad/      Unfinished optional input integration
experimental/  Offline navigation-metadata work and factory navigation tracing

Experimental metadata reception previously disrupted CarPlay reconnects.
It is excluded from installation. Its offline state reducer and ownership
tests are not a native driver fix or a working instruction publisher.

